+# Incident brief
+
+## 11 August 2026: stalled data ingest, full database disk
+
+**Impact:** customers saw stale dashboards for about two and a half hours overnight. No data was lost.
+**Root cause:** a malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; its logs filled the database disk.
+**Fix:** restarting ingest with the bad batch set aside, then freeing disk space.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80 percent: no owner named; open.
+- Stop bad batches jamming ingest: Jonas; open.
+- Faster paging escalation (15 unanswered minutes): Elif and Sunil; done (confirmed 30 September).
+- Handbook update: Mara; open.
+
+## 21 September 2026: public API outage
+
+**Impact:** the public API was unreachable for nearly all customers for 47 minutes.
+**Root cause:** its security certificate expired; automatic renewal had silently failed all month using an outdated access token.
+**Fix:** certificate renewed, API restarted.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Alert on renewal failures: done.
+- Reminder 14 days before each expiry: no owner named; open.
+- Alert on days left: no owner named; open.
+- Certificate check in weekly checklist: no owner named; open.
+- Incident handlers note their steps as they work: agreed.
+
+"Open" means no completion recorded in meeting notes through 30 September.
